The score beneath the story

Voice	It rings on	Its preparatory cue comes on
Bronze	3, 6, 9, …	2, 5, 8, …
Oak	4, 8, 12, …	3, 7, 11, …
Breath	5, 10, 15, …	4, 9, 14, …

The first shared strike after the count begins is beat 60, the least common multiple of 3, 4, and 5. Each preparation happens one beat before its strike, so the first shared preparation is beat 59. Iona solves the problem by shifting all three rhythms one beat earlier. The scrape, creak, and breath carry the calculation. The cord lets her feel it. And the answer is a chord the audience spends the whole story learning to expect, then gets to hear as silence.